<BaseLayout title="About | Neurinlab" description="Neurinlab studies and experiments with ways to use fast tools while keeping our thinking our own." lang="en" current="about">
  <section class="editorial-hero page-editorial-hero"><div class="wide-inner"><p class="editorial-kicker">Neurinlab's starting question</p><h1 class="editorial-title"><span>Making space to think</span><span>for ourselves</span></h1><p class="editorial-copy">Neurinlab studies and experiments with ways to use fast tools<br />while keeping our thinking and language our own.</p></div></section>
  <section class="dark-split"><div class="wide-inner split-editorial-grid"><h2>The question<br />behind Neurinlab</h2><p>AI makes it easier to produce answers, drafts, and summaries. But when an answer arrives before we have really stayed with the question, it can become harder to know what we actually think. Neurinlab begins there.</p></div></section>
  <section class="themes-section"><div class="wide-inner"><p class="section-label">What we study</p><div class="themes-grid"><article class="theme-item"><span>01</span><h2>AI and Thinking</h2><p>Before reaching for a quick answer, we stay with what we actually want to ask.</p></article><article class="theme-item"><span>02</span><h2>Writing in Our Own Words</h2><p>We return to fast drafts and shape them until the words feel like ours.</p></article><article class="theme-item"><span>03</span><h2>Ideas and Tools</h2><p>We gather scattered thoughts into structure and connect them to the next step.</p></article></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
